      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume this means an \"error scope\" (push/popErrorScope) error. That won\u0027t be the case for createBuffer - the error that causes it to return null (throw an exception in JS) is if it runs out of memory in the client-side mapping allocation, in the client-server model used by the spec and by dawn wire. If this happens then I don\u0027t believe we produce an error scope error, just return null: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/wire/client/Buffer.cpp;l\u003d49;drc\u003d7fdf446abc06f53adddc0c7cf4cb31b83e0507c5",
